        "language": "english",
        "review": "Lovely, tiny and aventurous. Lots of meaningful mechanics and items coupled with very wonky world generation ends up getting you extremely varied 30-ish minute runs. You may end up playing different games altogether depending on the randomness of the world. Sometimes your only goal is to get a boat so you'll want money and for that you could just sell the souls of goblins you painfully take down. Another world may have easily-accessible mines, which have many treasures inside but it might be tough to find a way out. Maybe you got a lot of HP and want to have a heir to inherit that or you got to accidentaly become a necromancer. Maybe you entered a tunnel that leads into endless darkness and you wander aimlessly until you die of old age. \n\nPretty fun nonetheless.",
